# Signing material — never committed, under any name.
# CI writes `app/android/keystore.jks` (flutter_build.yml) and Gradle reads
# `key.properties` / `key-dev.properties` / `key-stg.properties`, so the
# patterns are broad on purpose: a keystore named something else is still
# a keystore, and one accidental `git add -A` is all it takes.
*.jks
*.keystore
key.properties
key-*.properties

.cxx
.kotlin
